opentubex (0.37.1) stable; urgency=medium

  [ More improvements ]
  * Queued videos now show their length, music badge, views and upload date like
    playlist videos. A ⋮ menu moves or removes them, and dragging slides the
    other videos aside.
  * Removed the "Match top bar with main color" setting, which made the header
    hard to read with many themes
  * Added configurable SponsorBlock submission shortcuts, with ; to start or end
    a segment and ' to open the submission menu.
  * The buttons below the video are easier to tap on touch screens
  * Quick Settings now start with playback speed and watch history instead of
    language, region, main color and thumbnail size. If you never customized
    Quick Settings, you get the new set automatically.
  * DeArrow now has its own section in Add-ons settings, and SponsorBlock's
    excluded channels only appear while SponsorBlock is enabled.
  * Player settings are now grouped into sections, and long select labels are no
    longer cut off
  * The date, views and category below the video now use icons, like video
    cards.
  * Tooltips now use your theme's colors, font and corner rounding instead of
    the plain system style
  * F-Droid, SideStore, Flatpak and FlatPark listings now show what's new in
    each stable release, and the deb, rpm and AUR packages include it as their
    changelog
  * Dragging the seek bar shows a strip of frames around where you'll land, and
    fullscreen swipe-to-seek now shows the same seek bar preview instead of a
    popup in the middle of the screen.
  * Round icon buttons, such as Share, Refresh and the download actions, now use
    soft tinted backgrounds instead of bright filled circles with shadows
  * On Android, links from other sites shared with OpenTubeX now open with
    yt-dlp, and video links from popular sites such as Instagram, TikTok and
    Reddit can open directly in the app
  * Show verified and official artist badges, YouTube's search spelling
    corrections, the music credited in a video, shared community posts,
    information panels under videos, hashtag video and channel counts, and a
    Music tab on Trending
  * On Android, syncs now finish while the app is in the background, changes
    made while it is hidden reach your other devices without reopening it, and
    returning to the app no longer shows a false "Sync failed: timed out"
    message.
  * Press B to add the current video to your quick bookmark playlist or remove
    it, and Shift+S to save it to a playlist
  * Hashtag pages have a Shorts tab that keeps loading more Shorts
  * While dragging the seek bar, pull up past the middle of the strip of frames
    to seek precisely through longer videos, drag back down to return to normal
    seeking, and press Esc to cancel the drag.
  * Choose how much video loads ahead, stays loaded for rewinding, and must load
    before playing, with Data Saver, Default and Smooth Playback presets in
    Settings → Advanced → Buffering
  * New Always use backup media server setting in Advanced settings loads videos
    from YouTube's backup server right away, for example when your internet
    provider's cache is often slow
  * Import Playlists can import several YouTube Takeout playlist CSVs at once,
    with their original titles and descriptions when you also select
    playlists.csv
  * New Pause on Stream Recovery setting: when the player recovers from a stream
    error, it pauses and keeps the error on screen with a Copy button until you
    dismiss it
  * The Android and iOS apps keep tab thumbnails and channel avatars after a
    restart and show them offline, and you can see and clear this cache in
    Storage settings
  * The Seek history menu shows how long ago you left each position.
  * The Add to playlist prompt shows which videos you're adding, and its search,
    switches and sort fit in one row
  * Recommended for you now draws on your whole watch history and saved videos
    instead of repeating suggestions based on the same few videos, and uses more
    specific searches and topic labels
  * The comment filter and reload buttons are now the same size as the refresh
    button on the subscriptions pages
  * On Android, background tabs now stay loaded until memory runs low
    (adjustable in Advanced settings), tab previews no longer turn black while a
    page is loading, and the tab organizer button no longer stays highlighted
    after you pick a tab.
  * The Playback speed, Zoom, Volume boost and Theatre mode tiles in the player
    menu are highlighted while they are changed from their defaults
  * Sync finishes faster after small changes, and with an updated sync server, a
    watch history edit uploads only that entry instead of your whole history
  * The "Playing in Picture-in-Picture" message is now larger, centered on the
    player and shown with an icon

  [ Fixed bugs ]
  * Pinching on Android no longer zooms the app interface with WebViews such as
    Vanadium
  * With the custom title bar, middle-clicking the empty tab strip opens a tab
    again on Windows, maximized Settings no longer puts buttons under the window
    controls, the screen's top edge reaches the tabs of a maximized window, and
    the window controls no longer cover a Full Window video on Windows
  * Android: Fullscreen entered by rotating the phone stays on when the next
    video starts
  * The resolution menu lists every codec a video is available in, including
    ones your device can only decode in software, such as AV1 on GPUs without
    AV1 decoding.
  * Keep video tab titles when a channel loads behind the video, and restore
    channel names when returning to their pages
  * Fixed missing comments and video descriptions when Android restores an open
    video at startup.
  * Fixed repeated player reloads, videos failing to load without thumbnail
    previews, and broken channel lists when video or TV-show details are
    incomplete.
  * Fixed comment sorting and reload buttons looking enabled while offline.
  * Retry timed-out stream format checks before completing playlist preloading.
  * Fixed overflowing playlist thumbnail controls with a three-dot menu for
    reorder and remove actions. Playlist videos now show icon-labeled metadata
    like the queue and retain available view counts. Playlist positions appear
    in the top-left corner of each thumbnail.
  * Fixed unnecessary SABR player reloads caused by split stream headers and
    limited buffering of oversized stream responses.
  * Fixed gray watch-page action icons so they use the light or dark theme
    foreground color.
  * Videos played through Invidious no longer show a false age-restricted badge
  * Fixed Load More on Home stopping after 96 videos, downloaded playlist videos
    streaming online after Next, missing Shorts notifications on Android while
    the app is closed, missing notifications for channels outside the active
    profile, SRT files with dot timestamps failing to load, playlist searches
    carrying over to the next playlist, Yattee error toasts on videos with
    comments turned off, and hidden windows not returning from the macOS Dock.
  * The description's "...more" and copy buttons no longer show through the
    share menu and other video toolbar menus
  * With theatre as the default viewing mode, chapters, the transcript and
    SponsorBlock open below the video again when the watch page has no sidebar
  * Swiping between tabs on the app bar no longer makes the incoming page jump
    to a different scroll position on Android
  * Subscribing to a channel no longer opens its subscription settings when you
    only have one profile.
  * The player preview in Customize interface now shows the center play button
    and the player menu while playing, and matches the compact controls and menu
    on phones and narrow windows
  * Videos on Android and iOS no longer wait up to 25 seconds for a SABR
    countdown before they start playing.
  * On narrow screens, the buttons below the video now split into one row per
    group instead of wrapping with a stray divider
  * Android: yt-dlp playback works after a fresh install even when GitHub limits
    update requests, because the app bundles a current yt-dlp and updates it
    without GitHub's rate-limited API
  * Tab Organizer previews on Android no longer miss channel banners and avatars
    that load after the page.
  * Fixed Android downloads and other yt-dlp features disappearing when the
    saved download history file was empty
  * Videos now start when YouTube's assigned media server doesn't respond, for
    example an unreachable cache at your internet provider, because OpenTubeX
    switches to the backup server YouTube names
  * Volume, brightness and speed indicators appear over the video instead of the
    middle of the screen when the queue or another side panel is open in
    fullscreen
  * Links in update release notes open in your browser again, and imported
    settings, backups and remote content are handled more safely. Download
    templates and the IP block recovery script are no longer exported, backed up
    or synced
  * Fixed a thin line of the page showing between the minimized player and the
    navigation bar on Android when UI Scale isn't 100%
  * Fixed YouTube Takeout ZIP imports finding no data when the export was in a
    language other than English
  * Linux: OpenTubeX no longer shows a main process error when the desktop
    session starts it while D-Bus is still slow, such as when KDE Plasma
    restores the previous session at login, and KDE Wayland minimize detection
    now recovers in that case
  * Links in prompts, fullscreen player panels and expanded Super Chat messages
    open in your browser, and theme author links open once and follow your
    External Link Handling setting
  * Managed yt-dlp and FFmpeg downloads now say when antivirus software removed
    or blocked the downloaded file, and their error messages are translated
  * The Settings window header border no longer gets thinner after scrolling a
    settings page
  * Player submenu titles, including Caption Appearance, are now vertically
    centered in their headers
  * AiSList now hides or flags collaboration videos when any of their channels
    is on the list
  * Search results now show upload times for auto-generated Topic videos
  * The Shorts transcript panel no longer shows a second scrollbar or cuts off
    its last lines.
  * Jumping to a setting from Account activity no longer opens its help tooltip,
    which got stuck at the top of the window
  * Scheduled live streams and premieres now stay where they were announced in
    the New feed, Home, the Live tab and Invidious feeds when Show Scheduled
    Live Streams / Premieres First is off
  * The buttons at the bottom of the captions menu now have rounded corners that
    fit inside the player menu
  * Videos released to everyone after a members-only period now show their
    public release date in Subscriptions and Home recommendations
  * Pressing Esc while a dialog or the command palette is open over a fullscreen
    video now closes it instead of leaving the app stuck behind a cut-off dialog
  * Members-only videos no longer appear on channel pages, in search, related
    videos or Home unless you turn on "Members only" in that channel's
    subscription settings
  * The music visualizer no longer goes flat on Android when a track is played
    again after it ends
  * Seeking a paused video that still shows its thumbnail now shows the video at
    the new position
  * YouTube links in a channel's About tab open in OpenTubeX instead of the
    browser
  * The grid player menu no longer grows to the full height of the player, and
    its pages keep their header in view while you scroll long lists like audio
    tracks or caption languages
  * Videos no longer loop through the server countdown for minutes when YouTube
    stops sending media after the first minute
  * Recently ended live streams without any built-in formats now fall back to
    yt-dlp or show an error instead of leaving the player area empty
  * Fixed the app staying offline when a network blocks the internet check,
    Invidious playlists on the watch page stopping after the first page, and
    YouTube Takeout imports cutting video titles or adding extra text to video
    IDs

 -- OpenTubeX contributors <info@opentubex.org>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:32:04 +0000
